{"id": "EUVD-2026-82134", "enisaUuid": "558dd8b0-4506-386d-90ce-77cf5ef37b4a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/mana_ib: drain QP references after partial table insertion\n\nmana_table_store_ud_qp() publishes a QP at its send-queue id before\ninserting the receive-queue id, dropping the XArray lock between the two\nxa_insert_irq() calls. A concurrent completion handler can look up the QP\nand take a transient reference. When the second insertion fails, the\nrollback erased only the send-queue entry and returned, leaving both the\ninitial table reference and the transient reference outstanding while RDMA\ncore frees the QP, causing a use-after-free.\n\nDrain the reference as normal destruction does: drop the initial reference\nand wait for qp->free, releasing the QP only after every concurrent lookup\nreturns its reference.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:10:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:04:19", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4aaa2ab816c710be7385b31d08373edcdcd71656", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/638b9a5364c1482e5d104823c1a3884b3d249484", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/97f7c2262c28ebcae64fc957ee978646684a5ed9"], "aliases": ["GHSA-r87w-wp8m-2wvh", "CVE-2026-92513"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00c1e1cc-6e21-36de-8cf0-a6cfb61cb98a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "0739aae5-0d71-3f5e-8389-9fdb031e5f30", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8001e9257eca23264550ff9e34598ee43a80f0f9 <638b9a5364c1482e5d104823c1a3884b3d249484"}, {"id": "21ae15c2-5c51-36e7-bfb9-11232dd37823", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "4ddfce9e-7053-37fb-835c-329068176d9f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15"}, {"id": "93e12130-d956-3c9a-ac85-4ffa00bdfd6c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8001e9257eca23264550ff9e34598ee43a80f0f9 <97f7c2262c28ebcae64fc957ee978646684a5ed9"}, {"id": "97b666e3-101d-3358-bb82-0cf068bb566b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "a19f82e1-75b4-3289-84d0-6e758c62235b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "af9f4889-06e2-3f8f-8c1e-6827669deb82", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8001e9257eca23264550ff9e34598ee43a80f0f9 <4aaa2ab816c710be7385b31d08373edcdcd71656"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "cec091c4-a4f7-334e-ae7f-c81c25835c3e", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}